<title>CHINA: China's broad M2 money supply up 25.3 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>China's broad M2 money supply up 25.3 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's broad M2 money supply rose a year-on-year 25.3 percent in 1996, largely meeting a government target for the year of 25 percent, the Xinhua news agency quoted central bank governor Dai Xianglong as saying on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   1995	  1996</p>
<p> M2		30.0	  25.3 PERCENT</p>
<p> M1		18.0	  18.9</p>
<p> M0		14.0	  11.6</p>
<p>(Note: Data is year-on-year percentage growth. Year-ago figures are estimates.)</p>
</text>
